# Copy to site.local.env and fill in only what this machine needs.
#
#     cp common/site.local.env.example common/site.local.env
#
# site.local.env is NOT tracked, so every machine and every user keeps their
# own and they never collide in git. Leave a line out and discovery tries to
# find it; run
#
#     python3 common/check_site.py
#
# to see what was found and what was not.
#
# Format is strict KEY=value, one per line. It is read by both the Python
# stages and the shell runners, and it is NOT a shell script -- no command
# substitution, no logic. $HOME and $PROJECT (this checkout) are expanded;
# nothing else is.
#
# Anything you export before running still wins over this file.

# --- cluster: which partitions this account can actually submit to ----------
# sinfo lists every partition the cluster has; most of them you have no
# allocation on. Naming yours keeps them out of the prompt and, more
# importantly, out of the recommendation -- the emptiest partition on a shared
# cluster is usually the one nobody can use.
# PIPELINE_PARTITIONS=gpu_l40s,gpu_h200,gpu_h100
#
# One partition, chosen every run without asking:
# PIPELINE_PARTITION=gpu_l40s

# --- which kind of machine --------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to decide by whether sbatch is on PATH. Set it when that guess is
# wrong: a workstation that has Slurm installed, or a compute node already
# inside a job, where submitting more jobs is exactly wrong.
# PIPELINE_MODE=workstation

# --- sequence design --------------------------------------------------------
# MPNN_ROOT=$HOME/software/ProteinMPNN
# LIGANDMPNN_ROOT=$HOME/software/LigandMPNN
# LIGANDMPNN_CHECKPOINT=$LIGANDMPNN_ROOT/model_params/ligandmpnn_v_32_010_25.pt
#
# LigandMPNN's run.py needs torch, and the pipeline's own interpreter needs
# gemmi and numpy. One conda env can hold both -- which is why a workstation
# never needed this -- but where the environments are split, name the one with
# torch here:
# LIGANDMPNN_PYTHON=$HOME/software/ligandmpnn_venv/bin/python

# --- AlphaFold3, workstation ------------------------------------------------
# AF3_ROOT=$HOME/software/alphafold3
# MODEL_DIR=$HOME/software/alphafold3_model_params
# AF3_CONDA_ENV=alphafold3

# --- AlphaFold3, cluster ----------------------------------------------------
# AF3_WORKDIR=/scratch/<project>/<user>/software/alphafold

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Sequence databases for the full MSA pipeline. Unset means AF3 runs with
# --norun_data_pipeline, which is right for de novo designs with no homologs.
# DB_DIR=/path/to/af3/databases

# --- RFD3 -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Discovered from $CONDA_PREFIX and from software/rfd3/envs/*/bin/rfd3 beside
# the checkout. Set them here when it is somewhere else -- and note that a
# compute node has no activated environment, so "it works in my shell" is not
# evidence that a submitted job will find it.
# RFD3_EXE=/shared/scratch/<project>/<user>/software/rfd3/envs/rfd3_venv_py312/bin/rfd3
# CKPT=/shared/scratch/<project>/<user>/software/rfd3/checkpoints/rfd3_latest.ckpt
